NAME
     truncate - set a file's length

SYNOPSIS
     truncate [-c] -s SIZE FILE...
     fallocate -l LEN [-o OFFSET] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
     truncate sets each FILE to SIZE, which may be bigger than it is --
     the gap reads as zeroes and costs no blocks until something is
     written into it. SIZE may end in K, M or G, and may begin with + or
     - to mean relative to the length it has now.

     Called as fallocate, it reserves LEN bytes at OFFSET instead, so
     that a later write there cannot fail for want of space.

OPTIONS
     -s SIZE   the length to set
     -c        do not create a file that is not there
     -l LEN    fallocate: how much to reserve
     -o OFF    fallocate: where to start

SEE ALSO
     dd(1), du(1), stat(1)
